description:
Loads a published GeoZarr collection over a reference period and computes a WMO-style climatology — mean per day-of-year (1..366, optionally circular-smoothed) or per month (1..12), selected by `frequency` — then publishes the result as a new GeoZarr dataset with a `dayofyear` or `month` dimension.

Use it to derive normals from a dataset you have already ingested for the reference period — e.g. ingest chirps3_precipitation_daily for 1991-2020, then compute its day-of-year normal. (To compute ERA5-Land day-of-year normals without ingesting 30 years first, use the `era5land_temperature_daily_normal_1991_2020` / `era5land_precipitation_daily_normal_1991_2020` data sources, which read the reference period directly from the Earth Data Hub.)

The `output_dataset_id` must have a registered data source on the instance: a dataset template in `plugins/datasets/` with `sync: {kind: static}` and a `display` block (colormap/range). No ingestion plugin is required — the data is produced by this workflow.

Zarr output cannot be produced synchronously, so run this as a batch job (`POST /jobs`, then `POST /jobs/{id}/results`):

{
  "normal": {
    "process_id": "climate_normal",
    "arguments": {
      "dataset_id": "chirps3_precipitation_daily",
      "output_dataset_id": "chirps3_precipitation_daily_normal_1991_2020",
      "variable": "precip",
      "temporal_extent": ["1991-01-01", "2020-12-31"],
      "frequency": "dayofyear",
      "smoothing_window": 31
    },
    "result": true
  }
}
